# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own Discord Application ID.
#
# You do not have to do this by hand — on first launch Statusify shows a setup
# wizard that asks for the ID and writes .env for you. This file exists for
# anyone who would rather configure it up front, or who is deploying the app
# somewhere the wizard cannot run.
#
# Create an application at https://discord.com/developers/applications, then
# copy the "Application ID" from the General Information page. It is a long
# numeric snowflake, not the bot token, and it is not a secret in the usual
# sense — but .env is gitignored anyway so it never lands in a commit.
DISCORD_APP_ID=
